= Attendance
Attendance is not directly included in the calculation of your course grade. However, regular attendance is strongly encouraged, as students who attend class consistently are generally better prepared to succeed in the course. Please note that graded in-class activities, such as quizzes, group work, or tests, may affect your course grade if you are absent when they are administered.

If a student misses a class, they should obtain the notes and any announcements or assignments from a classmate. If an illness, bereavement, or other significant personal circumstance prevents a student from attending class, completing an assignment, or taking a quiz or exam, they should contact the instructor (and possibly the Dean of Students) as soon as possible. It may be possible to adjust due dates/exam dates in particular circumstances, so please reach out if those should occur.

