= Honor System
All graded work submitted in this course must represent the student's own work and understanding. Students may discuss homework and quiz material with classmates and with the instructor. However, when preparing work to be submitted for grading, each student must work independently and must write the solution in their own words and based on the student's own understanding.

Students may not consult partial or complete solutions to assigned problems that have been prepared by someone else while completing graded work. This includes, but is not limited to, solutions prepared by current or former instructors or students at Virginia Tech or elsewhere, whether the solutions are available online or through other sources. The Honor Code applies to all graded work in this course.

Notes, assignments, quizzes, tests, exams, solutions, and other materials distributed or generated for this course are intended for use *only by students enrolled in this CRN during the current semester. Without written permission from the instructor, students may not distribute, post online, or otherwise make such materials available to anyone who is not enrolled in this section during the current semester.* This includes uploading course materials, tests, or solutions to websites or other online platforms. The prohibition on sharing solutions applies regardless of who originally prepared the solution.

