= Artificial Intelligence
The use of generative AI tools, including ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and similar systems, is not permitted on graded coursework unless explicitly authorized by the instructor.

All submitted work must represent the student's own mathematical reasoning and understanding. Students may not use generative AI to generate, solve, rewrite, or substantially modify solutions that are submitted for homework, quizzes, exams, or other graded assessments.

Generative AI tools may be used for general studying and learning outside of graded coursework, provided that such use does not circumvent the requirements of an assignment or assessment. However, the instructor does not believe such tools are in your best interest as a learner. It is crucial you build foundational knowledge of the subject without these tools since they may be wrong, and there are so many existing alternatives to support you in this class. Instead, it is highly encouraged that students reach out to the many free, human resources available to them through the university before using AI tools. Further, so many extra practice problems already exist and do not need to be generated: WebAssign's practice tools, Paul's Online Notes, the problems in our textbook (or any calc 2 textbook!), etc. Please see the Resources section above for more information, or email the instructor if you need help finding such resources, they would be happy to direct you.

For all intents and purposes in this course, large language models and other forms of generative AI are considered people not enrolled in this course. This means that under no circumstances can such programs be used to generate complete or partial solutions to problems given. Similarly, making any class materials available to such programs is not allowed.

The use of generative AI on graded work is considered the use of an external aid. When such use has not been authorized by the instructor, it may constitute a violation of the Virginia Tech Honor Code. Students who are uncertain whether a particular use of AI is permitted should consult the instructor before submitting the work


